{
  "codec": "ontos-codec-v1",
  "description": "measure (ontos-codec.md §10, design record 0008, ontos issue 35): a value's canonical encoded length (encoded_bytes), its expanded occurrence count (occurrences) and its height, computed without expanding shared subtrees and checked against bounds the caller states. Hand-authored (Class A): every expected number is computed from the equations of §10.1, never from an implementation, and each case's note shows the arithmetic. NOT part of the byte corpus: vectors/codec.json is that, and the CLIs never read this file. A value is written as a node table, {\"nodes\": [{\"atom\": \"<hex>\"} | {\"tuple\": [<earlier node index>, ...]}, ...], \"root\": <index>}: a tuple names only earlier nodes, so the table is acyclic, and an index may appear more than once. A face that can share builds one in-memory node per table entry, so a node named twice is one shared node. Each face measures the root under `bounds` (one bound per measure, each at most 2^53 - 1) and MUST produce `expect`: either {\"measures\": the three exact measures}, when every measure is within its bound (less than or equal to it), or {\"exceeded\": the identifiers of every measure over its bound, in ascending order}. `expandable` is true when the expanded tree has at most 4096 occurrences: a face that cannot share subtrees (Rust) builds such a value by copying, and replays only those cases.",
